<p>I figure there are two options:</p>
<p>1: We have, but it didn't add anything useful to the containment procedures, so it's not detailed here.<br />
2: We haven't, because we've already got this thing successfully contained, and the need to learn more about it comes secondary to the need to contain it, and since we don't know what -2 or -3 might do as the result of intrusion by air, it might be best to stay out.</p>
